# Brutal Cathar's enters trigger takes only a creature an opponent controls: Bot1's own Ornithopter and Bot2's Mox Ruby
# (not a creature) are refused as targets, Bot2's Ornithopter is exiled (not its Dryad Arbor, a land creature, which
# stays). Daybound shows on the Cathar while it is day, and the day face has no ward: Bot2 bolts it paying nothing, and
# the exiled Ornithopter comes back under Bot2's control (CR 610.3, 400.7).

[Dice]
1; 1; 1; 1; 1; 1
[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Brutal Cathar
Ornithopter
Island x20
[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Ornithopter
Dryad Arbor
Lightning Bolt
Island x20
[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Dryad Arbor.Play
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Brutal Cathar.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Exile = Ornithopter
? DayNight = Day
? Bot1.Battlefield.Brutal Cathar.Keywords = Daybound
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Brutal Cathar)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[Expect]
Exile.Count = 0
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 0
Bot2.Battlefield.Dryad Arbor.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Brutal Cathar
Bot2.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt
